              SignalsWorkspacePage.)

Shape of the parity unit (apps/parity/parity-manifest.json id=page:telemetry/SignalDiff)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
requiredCount=23 = 5 panels + 3 data-states + 15 strings. 0 charts, 0 maps. Data sources (5):
useVehicles (GET /vehicles), useSignals (GET /signals/{id}/available), useSignalDiffServer
(GET /signals/{id}/diff), usePinned (GET /pinned), useTogglePin (POST /pinned + DELETE /pinned/{id}).
The web page is a thin orchestrator composing the shared SignalCompareControls + SignalDiffTable +
BulkActionsToolbar inside a PageContainer; the native port reproduces the whole tree and composes the
already-ported shared surfaces (SignalCompareControls, BulkActionsToolbar, PageContainer) and the shared
SignalDiffProjection rather than re-implementing them.

Native realisation (Fluent / WinUI 3, ADR-002/004/005/006/011/013/014/015)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
- SignalDiffPage : UserControl — mounts the shared SharedSurfaces.PageContainer (title / subtitle, the
  "Share" TsCopyLinkButton in the header Actions) whose PageContent is the full diff tree: the shared
  SignalCompareControls bar (Window A / Window B pickers + presets + name filter + the eight category
  chips, with the page-local vehicle picker — a labelled TsSelect — mounted in its TopSlot), the four
  diff TsStatCards (Changed-signals / Visible-after-filter / Pinned / Window-span), the shared
  BulkActionsToolbar (Pin / Unpin / Copy CSV / Add-as-alert), the load-failed TsAlertBanner, and the diff
  TsGlassPanel with its loading-skeleton / no-changes-empty / selectable pinned-first rows (a checkbox +
  per-row pin toggle + name + Window A / Window B + coloured Δ + L1/L2/LOG source badges) + the
  pinned-chips footer. Thin renderer: every label/value/visibility flows from SignalDiffPageDisplay;
  PropertyChanged is marshalled onto the UI thread; Group automation peer; tokens only (no literal colours).
- SignalDiffPageViewModel : INotifyPropertyChanged — UI-thread-free state holder. Reads the fleet vehicles
  (useVehicles) and auto-picks the first when none is selected, fetches the catalog (useSignals), the diff
  (useSignalDiffServer) and the pins (usePinned) through ISignalDiffPageFeed, owns the name/category filter
  + multi-row selection + the two compare windows, and the pin/unpin + bulk pin/unpin flow (useTogglePin).
  LoadAsync/RefreshAsync/SetVehicleAsync/LoadVehicleDataAsync + superseding CTS; no I/O in the view.
- SignalDiffPageProjection / SignalDiffPageModel / SignalDiffPageDisplay — pure projection (no WinUI types)
  resolving all 15 i18n keys on every call, the four stat-card values (fmtInt + windowSpan ports reused
  from SignalsWorkspaceProjection), the category-then-name filtered + pinned-first-sorted rows (reusing the
  shared SignalDiffProjection so this page and the unified workspace stay in lockstep), and the
  loading/empty/error/rows data-state flags. SignalDiffVehicle.ParseList ports useVehicles tolerantly.
- ISignalDiffPageFeed / EmptySignalDiffPageFeed / SignalDiffPageClientFeed — the data port + the no-backend
  default the shell-registered page hosts itself against + the generated-contract-client adapter (ADR-004):
  GET /vehicles, GET /signals/{id}/available, GET /signals/{id}/diff, GET /pinned, POST /pinned,
  DELETE /pinned/{id}. The diff read uses the backend's default trailing-hour window (the generated
  /signals/{id}/diff descriptor declares no at_a/at_b query params — the same compromise as the sibling
  SignalDiffTableSource and SignalsWorkspaceClientFeed); the window-span stat still reflects the user windows.
- Navigation: RouteTable.cs already maps Page("SignalDiff","signal-diff",RouteGroup.TelemetrySignals,"Signal
  Diff"); ShellWindow.xaml.cs registers PageFactory.Register("SignalDiff", () => new SignalDiffPage()).
- i18n: the platform catalog (apps/windows/Strings/en/Resources.resw) already carries all 15 required keys;
  the select-all checkbox Narrator name (signalDiff.selectAll) resolves through the in-code English fallback,
  exactly as the already-shipped sibling SignalDiffTable surface does — no catalog change is required.

